Public variables - are the API.
Private ones are the implementation.
We later will learn how to add an HTML file that will include the API (We will avoid mentioning private variables)

Minimal API:
Every object is born in order to fill some defined job, and it fills it for other objects and all the objects (beside main) provides service to some other object.
so think about the classes as clients, each need serve the other and eventually other programmers.

The guideline for minimal API is KEEP IT SIMPLE, whatever your API does it should do exactly only that!
Don't over-add shit.